te — fiscal dominance plus correlated repricing plus degraded plumbing, observed jointly in 1973-74, 1980-82, 1987 and 2022. This is the one conjunction in the set where a heavy discount is the error.\nJOINT = 0.37 x 0.42 + 0.50 x sqrt(0.37x0.63x0.42x0.58) = 0.1554 + 0.50 x 0.2383 = 0.2746 -> 27.\nCOHERENCE WITH CQ4's VARIANCE AND WITH CQ6-C/D MASS, as the lock demands: my CQ4 range 0.85-3.80 with a P90 1.85pp above a market-pinned anchor is a high-rate-variance distribution, which is the same object as conjunct A — a 27 would be incoherent with a narrow CQ4. And CQ5's conjunct B requires the C-type (inflationary/fiscal-solvency) crash rather than the D-type (disinflationary bust): my C at 22 against D at 13 makes the non-rallying crash the more probable of the two crisis cells, which supports 27 and is why I cannot sit at the Scout's 13 while also holding C > D.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:57.369Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"Turkiye annual CPI (TurkStat, December print) averages below 8.0%/yr over calendar 2028-2031 AND Mexico's headline CPI (INEGI) averages below 3.5% over the same four years. Both required, so a single good Turkish year does not trigger it.\",\"by_when\":\"Feb 28, 2032 (full-year 2031 releases)\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the single load-bearing term in my CQ2: the five high-inflation OECD-38 members contributing ~0.70pp to GDP-weighted core. That contribution would fall toward ~0.40pp and my 2027-2036 aggregate from 2.65% to ~2.35%. CQ2 conjunct A falls from 0.64 to ~0.42 and CQ2 from 32 to ~21; CQ6-C falls from 22 to ~16 and CQ6-D rises from 13 to ~18, with B absorbing the balance; CQ4 P50 falls ~0.15pp to ~2.05; hypothesis plank (c) rises from 45 to ~58. My whole divergence from the Historian's CQ2 of 14 would stand revealed as a weighting convention rather t